#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_numeric

#% text
# `is_numeric(x)` is `true` when `x` is a number, or an expression without unknowns that evaluates numerically to a number (`pi`, `sqrt(2) + 1`), and `false` otherwise.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_numeric(pi)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_numeric(sqrt(2) + sin(1))
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_numeric(x + 1)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
select([e, 8, a, b, 20, 1.4], is_numeric)
#% output
#= [e, 8, 20, 1.4]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The parameter type `numeric` applies the same test: `fn g(w: numeric) = ...` defines `g` only for numeric arguments, so `g(w)` with a symbol stays unevaluated until numbers are put in (as in a plot or `find_root`).

#% cell
fn gq(w: numeric) = n_integrate(sin(w*r), [r, 0, 1]); [gq(pi), gq(w)]
#% output
#= [0.6366197723675815, gq(w)]

